 "seesTitle": "What Platja des Trenc (Ses Covetes) sees",
 "seesHTML": "Looking WNW from the sand, the sight line threads a gap: Cap Blanc's cliffs at ~277\u00b0 and the Tramuntana beyond 300\u00b0 both miss the sun's path. What remains is the low Marina de Llucmajor plateau, 17\u201319 km away and only 0.25\u20130.30\u00b0 high \u2014 totality rides \u22481.8\u00b0, some 3\u00bd sun-widths, above it. The cost of beach level: the final partial phase slips behind that plateau at \u224820:44, a minute before true sunset. Expect the biggest crowd on the island.",
 "capHTML": "Horizon panorama from Platja des Trenc (Ses Covetes): terrain silhouettes with projected angular altitudes against the sun's descent. The crescent is last visible at \u224820:44.",
 "recoTitle": "Around Platja des Trenc (Ses Covetes)",
 "recoHTML": "<li><b>The open beach west of Ses Covetes</b> \u2014 clear of the pine line; arrive early for parking, which sells out on normal August evenings.</li><li><b>Es Caragol or the Presos cliff</b> \u2014 the nearest sun-into-the-sea upgrades (click their rows).</li>",
 "verdictText": "Totality with 1.8\u00b0 to spare \u2014 terrain takes the crescent at \u224820:44"
